From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Zuasti <rzuasti@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:03:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: acknowledge messages once the client handled them

Manager::receive_messages_unacknowledged yields each message with its
Acknowledgement, to send once the client stored it: the server sends
unacknowledged messages again on the next connection, so quitting or
crashing before then no longer loses them. Messages handled here and not
yielded are acknowledged here. Manager::receive_messages acknowledges
each message as it is yielded, after it was saved.

A message decrypted before but not acknowledged comes back as
DuplicatedMessage; it is skipped and acknowledged, logged at debug.

Requires MessagePipe::stream_unacknowledged from libsignal-service.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
